.TH DCC-COMPONENT 8 2026-11-26 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-component \- switch parts of Dudes Control Center on or off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-component
.BR enable | disable
.BR fan | cpu | keyboard
.br
.B dcc-component ec\-direct
.BR enable | disable
.br
.B dcc-component status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc-component
switches the fan, CPU or keyboard part of Dudes Control Center on or off
and keeps that choice across reboots and package updates.
The Settings tab of
.BR dcc-gui (1)
runs it through
.BR pkexec (1);
polkit asks for the administrator password (action
.BR org.dudes-control-center.component ).
.TP
.B disable
Writes the flag file
.IR /etc/dudes-control-center/disabled- <component>
and stops the part's units.
The units carry
.B ConditionPathExists=!
on that file, so systemd does not start them again.
.TP
.B enable
Removes the flag file and starts the units.
.TP
.B ec\-direct enable\fR|\fBdisable
Allows or forbids direct EC access through the I/O ports 0x62/0x66 for
laptops where the
.BR dcc_fan (4)
module does not load (no Clevo WMI interface), then restarts the fan daemon
(unless fan control is switched off).
It is off by default: without the module and without this, the fan daemon only
monitors, the firmware controls the fans and nothing is written to the EC.
.IP
.B Warning:
the ports are written with the register layout of Clevo laptops. On a laptop
with another layout these writes can change charging, power or thermal
settings, stop the fans or overheat the hardware. Use it only on Clevo-based
laptops, at your own risk. Even when allowed, the daemon and
.BR dcc-fan-cli (1)
first read the EC and refuse the ports unless it answers like a Clevo EC
(steady CPU temperature register, close to the CPU's own sensor; fan speed
registers in a fan's range).
The GUI's switch asks for a confirmed warning first.
.TP
.B status
Prints one line per part:
.IR component " " enabled | disabled ,
and
.BR "ec-direct enabled" | disabled .
Needs no root.
.SS Units per part
.TP
.B fan
dcc-fan-daemon.service
.TP
.B cpu
dcc-cpu-daemon.service, dcc-hard-limit-enforcer.service and .timer
.TP
.B keyboard
dcc-kbd-daemon.service
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when run without root, 2 for an unknown action or part.
.SH NOTES
Switching
.B fan
off leaves the fans at 100\~% until the next reboot (the fan service's stop
fail-safe); after the reboot the firmware controls them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR /etc/dudes-control-center/disabled-fan ", " disabled-cpu ", " disabled-keyboard
Flag files.
.TP
.I /etc/dudes-control-center/ec-direct-access
Contains
.B enabled
while direct EC access is allowed.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.dudes-control-center.component.policy
polkit action.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sudo dcc-component disable keyboard
Stop the keyboard daemon; the LEDs keep their last colors.
.TP
.B dcc-component status
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-gui (1),
.BR dcc-fan-daemon (8),
.BR dcc-cpu-daemon (8),
.BR dcc-kbd-daemon (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
